{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4df","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a070a7-9081-7d73-bd3a-2f4da2eb7b1c"},"sequence":202,"recorded_at":1780531400000399,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d1923f0-6c67-41a3-89b5-230e3cfe396c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5d1923f0-6c67-41a3-89b5-230e3cfe396c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d1923f0-6c67-41a3-89b5-230e3cfe396c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"f45deffd-1772-4f55-ba49-cfede6b64280"},"task_id":"f45deffd-1772-4f55-ba49-cfede6b64280","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"f45deffd-1772-4f55-ba49-cfede6b64280","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1727 line(s) above)\n1728|### Refusal guard inventory\n1729|\n1730|Six rounds of review closed one guard at a time, and the seventh found the twin\n1731|of the sixth one file away: `decodeExitStatus` was swept over 0..255 while the\n1732|reader-side gate in `Read` stayed at four sampled values. Working from memory\n1733|closes the guard you were told about. This table is the forced traversal that\n1734|replaces memory, and it is derived rather than written: `TestTheRefusalGuardInventoryIsDerivedFromTheReaderSource`\n1735|parses every refusal site out of `internal/cliresult/client.go` and requires a\n1736|bijection with the rows below, so a guard added without a row - or a row whose\n1737|site no longer exists - is a red before a reviewer has to find it.\n1738|\n1739|Every row states what its domain evidence actually is. `measured` means the\n1740|guard was driven across its whole domain and the admitted and refused counts are\n1741|asserted against a production enumeration. `stated bound` means part of the\n1742|domain is not driven and names the contract reason, never effort.\n1743|\n1744|| # | Guard | Sentinel | Refusal marker | Domain evidence | Measured by |\n1745|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1746|| 1 | `Read` refuses an exit status Section 15.2 assigns no meaning | `ErrUnregisteredExitStatus` | `%w: %d` | measured over 0..255 and eight values outside the byte range, admission required to agree with `ExitStatusMeaning` at every point | `TestTheReadLevelExitStatusAdmissionIsSweptOverTheWholeDomain`, `TestTheReadLevelExitStatusAdmissionAdmitsARealReadingAtEveryRegisteredStatus` |\n1747|| 2 | `Read` refuses a document belonging to some other contract | `ErrForeignDocument` | `schema %q` | measured over every contract identifier the pinned catalog registers plus twelve near-miss neighbours of the two admitted ones; stated bound - the member's domain is every JSON string and a discriminator fails on a neighbour of what it admits, not on an arbitrary string | `TestTheForeignSchemaRefusalIsMeasuredOverTheRegisteredContractVocabulary` |\n1748|| 3 | `documentSchema` reports stdout that carries no document | `ErrAbsentDocument` | `%w: %s` | measured at every registered exit status, and required at each to be distinct from the read-failure and foreign-contract facts | `TestReadDistinguishesAbsenceFromAReadFailure`, `TestTheReadLevelExitStatusAdmissionIsSweptOverTheWholeDomain` |\n1749|| 4 | `documentSchema` reports stdout that is not readable JSON | `ErrUnreadableDocument` | `decode: %v` | measured on a truncated envelope and on non-JSON bytes, each required to be distinct from an absence | `TestReadDistinguishesAbsenceFromAReadFailure` |\n1750|| 5 | `documentSchema` refuses a second document on stdout | `ErrUnreadableDocument` | `more than one document` | measured on two concatenated conforming envelopes, required to be answered by this guard and not by the common-data-model gate that also refuses those bytes | `TestReadDistinguishesAbsenceFromAReadFailure` |\n1751|| 6 | `documentSchema` refuses bytes with more than one reading | `ErrUnreadableDocument` | `outside the Section 1.6 common logical data model` | measured over every declared member of both schemas and over a conforming document several thousand bytes long; stated bound - the number half of Section 1.6 is not enforced on this path, disclosed below and pinned | `TestADuplicateSchemaMemberCannotSelectTheBranch`, `TestTheCommonDataModelGateDoesNotCoverTheSection16NumberRule` |\n1752|| 7 | `documentSchema` refuses a document with no `schema` member | `ErrUnreadableDocument` | `document has no schema member` | measured over its two-valued presence domain, both values driven; stated bound - a predicate keyed on the exit status survives, and the exit status is not a dimension of Section 14.2's exactly-one-document rule | `TestReadDistinguishesAbsenceFromAReadFailure` |\n1753|| 8 | `documentSchema` refuses a `schema` member that is not a string | `ErrUnreadableDocument` | `schema member is not a string` | measured over every JSON value form, JSON `null` included, with a string control required to reach the discriminator instead | `TestTheSchemaMemberTypeGuardIsMeasuredOverEveryJSONValueForm` |\n1754|| 9 | `readSuccess` refuses a success object at a failure status | `ErrOutcomeDisagreement` | `carries a CLI Result, which reports success` | measured over all seventeen registered failure statuses, the count asserted against `axerror.IsFailureExitStatus` | `TestReadRefusesEveryDisagreementBetweenStdoutAndTheExitStatus` |\n1755|| 10 | `readSuccess` refuses a document claiming a command the invocation did not run | `ErrOutcomeDisagreement` | `stdout reports command %q` | measured over all 1,936 ordered pairs of the 44 registered tags, classified 18 admitted / 306 by this guard / 1,144 before stdout is read / 468 by the version binding; stated bound - for a pair involving one of the 26 unimplemented tags an earlier named refusal settles it | `TestTheCommandAgreementGuardOwnsAMeasuredShareOfTheTagVocabulary` |\n1756|| 11 | `readFailure` refuses a failure object at exit 0 | `ErrOutcomeDisagreement` | `carries a Structured Error, which reports failure` | declared subsumed - `decodeExitStatus` never admits `exit_code` 0, so row 12 refuses the same input one guard later; the harness carries the mutant and records it as subsumed rather than killed | `TestReadRefusesEveryDisagreementBetweenStdoutAndTheExitStatus` |\n1757|| 12 | `readFailure` refuses an `exit_code` unequal to the observed status | `ErrOutcomeDisagreement` | `must equal that error's exit_code` | measured over all seventeen registered failure statuses for a code the pinned registry does not carry, which is the class where this guard is the sole enforcement | `TestTheExitStatusEqualityBindsACodeTheRegistryDoesNotCarry` |\n1758|\n1759|Row 8 changed production code when it was measured. `encoding/json` admits JSON\n1760|`null` into a `string` and yields `\"\"`, so a document whose `schema` member was\n1761|`null` had been answered as a foreign contract carrying the schema `\"\"` - a\n1762|claim that some other contract owns the document, when what is true is that this\n1763|one is not readable. The guard now checks the raw token alongside the unmarshal.\n1764|\n1765|The guards this leaf added or reordered outside that file are listed with it,\n1766|because the twin one file away is exactly what a single-file table would have\n1767|missed again:\n1768|\n1769|| Guard | File | Function | Measured by |\n1770|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1771|| The registered-status admission inside the document - the twin of row 1 | `internal/axerror/decode.go` | `decodeExitStatus` | `TestTheExitStatusAdmissionIsSweptOverEveryByteValue` |\n1772|| The common-data-model gate added to the failure branch | `internal/axerror/decode.go` | `requireCommonDataModel` | `TestDecodeRefusesADuplicateMemberOnEveryDeclaredMember` |\n1773|| The code-to-exit-status agreement | `internal/axerror/decode.go` | `decodeBody` | `TestTheCodeToExitStatusAgreementIsMeasuredOverTheWholeCodeRegistry` |\n1774|| The envelope identity settled before the closed member set | `internal/axerror/decode.go` | `Decode` | `TestUnsupportedMajorIsSettledBeforeTheClosedMemberRule` |\n1775|| The same reordering on the success branch | `internal/cliresult/decode.go` | `Decode` | `TestUnsupportedMajorIsSettledBeforeTheClosedMemberRule` |\n1776|| The unsupported-major comparison reached through `Read` | `internal/cliresult/decode.go` | `verifyEnvelopeIdentity` | `TestTheUnsupportedMajorGuardIsSweptOverAMeasuredMajorRange` |\n1777|| The fan-in projection's unregistered-version refusal | `internal/axerror/registry.go` | `CodesByExitStatus` | `TestCodesByExitStatusRefusesAnUnregisteredVersion` |\n1778|\n1779|STATED BOUND of the inventory itself: the derivation is exhaustive over\n1780|`internal/cliresult/client.go`, which this leaf added in full. The second table\n1781|is enumerated rather than derived, and the refusals `internal/axerror/decode.go`,\n1782|`internal/axerror/registry.go` and `internal/cliresult/decode.go` carry from\n1783|earlier leaves are those leaves' inventories, not this one's. Both tables are\n1784|pinned: every named function must be declared in its named file and every named\n1785|test must exist as a declaration, so a rename is a red rather than a row\n1786|pointing at nothing.\n1787|\n1788|Two disclosures the traversal produced, stated here because neither is visible\n1789|from a passing suite.\n1790|\n1791|The Section 1.6 common-data-model gate does NOT enforce the number half of that\n1792|section. `canonicaljson.Canonicalize` refuses duplicate members, non-UTF-8, and\n1793|non-canonical encoding, and the doc comment on `documentSchema` enumerates what\n1794|it owns; the opening sentence \"inside the Section 1.6 common logical data model\"\n1795|overstated it. `Read` admits a Structured Error whose `details` carry `1.5`,\n1796|which SPEC.md forbids as \"integers only, inside the IEEE 754 double\n1797|safe-integer range\". Section 1.6's number rule is bound to `internal/scalar` and\n(more lines below)"}}}
