{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c56f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a070a7-9081-7d73-bd3a-2f4da2eb7b1c"},"sequence":274,"recorded_at":1780531400000543,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d1923f0-6c67-41a3-89b5-230e3cfe396c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5d1923f0-6c67-41a3-89b5-230e3cfe396c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d1923f0-6c67-41a3-89b5-230e3cfe396c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"17dedd22-1589-4123-91be-06dae7de5bdd"},"task_id":"17dedd22-1589-4123-91be-06dae7de5bdd","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"17dedd22-1589-4123-91be-06dae7de5bdd","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1964 line(s) above)\n1965|sections carry. One binding is `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\n1966|native-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by the positive\n1967|`TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` lanes together\n1968|with the negative `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` legacy\n1969|refusal arm), three are\n1970|`partial` (Section 14.2 at 8/9, bound to\n1971|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult), whose undischarged clause `14.2#6`\n1972|is the process exit status this repository has no binary to produce; and\n1973|Section 15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\n1974|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\n1975|the RPC hello obligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\n1976|binds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\n1977|TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no RPC\n1978|hello frame and no provider plugin, and advertises no Structured Error as a\n1979|TerminalBackend capability. The closed 16-capability admission registry in\n1980|[`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) gates which operations\n1981|an admitted probe may confer; it is never advertised on an RPC hello path and\n1982|carries no Structured Error code, so the prohibition holds vacuously and the\n1983|clause stays undischarged. The same package carries the Section 4 lifecycle,\n1984|attach, entrypoint, replication, and historical-translation conformance\n1985|harness (`conformance.go`, exercised by `conformance_test.go`) and an\n1986|AST-derived refusal-arm inventory (`refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`) that\n1987|requires every production refusal arm to resolve to a named asserting test\n1988|in both directions, so a refusal that ships unwitnessed fails the suite),\n1989|one is\n1990|`sliver` (Section 10.3, whose chunk offset invariant is\n1991|enforced by `validateBlobDescriptor` while its two receiver clauses have no\n1992|implementation), three are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\n1993|which carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\n1994|and forty-one are `unevidenced`. Two sections are recorded unowned.\n1995|Assigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2` and\n1996|nothing else; every other assignment is refused with its ratio and its gap.\n1997|A `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\n1998|`unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\n1999|\n2000|One admitted binding out of forty-nine covers a single clause, and it is\n2001|disclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\n2002|ever be exercised synthetically. Its discharge is no longer positive-only: the\n2003|native-Windows lanes carry the positive arm and\n2004|`TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` the legacy refusal arm,\n2005|both registered against the `config-versioned-readers` acceptance case.\n2006|\n2007|That is a disclosure of the shipped state, not a target that was met.\n2008|`TestRunRefusesEveryAssignedSectionThatOnlySlivers` and\n2009|`TestVerifyAssignedSectionsRefusesEveryBindingThatOnlySlivers` pin every failing\n2010|binding with its exact measured ratio, so a section that becomes covered has to\n2011|leave those tables deliberately. Five further gaps the disclosure surfaced:\n2012|Section 15.2's code-to-exit registry is implemented in\n2013|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) and checked row by row, and\n2014|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult) now maps a failure to that exact\n(more lines below)"}}}
